        <id>https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41036</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/content/pull/41036"/>
        <updated>2025-09-05T23:38:52.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7466?v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/><h3 dir="auto">Description</h3>
<p dir="auto">Clarify that Safari does not intend to support custom<strong>ized</strong> built-in elements, leaving it clear that Safari <em>does</em> support "custom" elements.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Motivation</h3>
<p dir="auto">This note was unclear to me on first reading.</p>
<h3 dir="auto">Additional details</h3>
<ul dir="auto">
<li><a href="https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/custom-elements.html" rel="nofollow">HTML Standard § 4.13 Custom elements</a> is consistent in its use of "custom" vs "customized" when referring to autonomous vs built-in elements, respectively.</li>
</ul>
